kly have been increasingly  hiding the data and hiding the  information as the situation's got worse  when you should absolutely be doing the  absolute opposite dr. Samir Sinha at the  National Institute on Aging suggests  there's no room for gaps in information  that could lead to poor decisions  considering 8 in 10 covered 19 deaths  have happened to people in long-term  care the system that cost Canadians 22  billion dollars a year  Ross Laura Global News Halifax in part  to Ross explores what the future of  long-term care might look like including  legislated standards and the possibility  of a greater role for the federal  government that's tomorrow on global  national up next blackout Tuesday social  media going dark for a cause  people all over the world are showing  solidarity for the protests in the US  and many are supporting blackout Tuesday  social media movement started by the  music industry black squares filled news  feeds it wasn't a perfect campaign and  some activists have questioned whether  it's done more harm than good but as  Heather Eurex West explains the act of  online solidarity hasn't gone unnoticed  these are people in Calgary Rudy  balligan has been having a lot of heavy  conversations about race lately with his  9 year old son  the Calgary father says it's always a  concern when he grows up if he gets in a  situation or he gets pulled over by the  cops he's going to be a black child is  that can affect him for work or  opportunities the death of George Floyd  and others has brought up so much pain  for many in the black community when I  first saw it to be honest with you I  cried I was sitting on my couch my jaw  was wide open and as time went on I  might just tears filled my face so when  the talent manager saw the music  industry was taking a moment to pause  and reflect this week he knew it was the  right thing to do a lot of those music  that we make is about you know social  awareness about struggle about personal  you know perseverance and you know it  doesn't matter really what genre music  has always been that healing force  streaming services like Apple music  replaced browsing and regular  programming with a radio stream Tuesday  celebrating the best in black music well  across social media black squares began  to take over feeds it may be small just  for the signs of solidarity still what  may have been a well-intentioned flood  of support wasn't without controversy as  one sociologist pointed out on Twitter  why would you want the black lives  matter or BLM hashtag to be flooded with  black squares erasing people's activism  author Blair Imani agreed all this is  doing is flooding the BLM hashtags with  pointless black squares and burying  important information you can write your  message in texts don't add a hashtag but  don't stop because controversy aside to  people like Chris Steffler this black  out Tuesday initiative has meant a lot I  know that as a black man  as a black Canadian and this is a black  person when I see so many of my white  friends on Instagram posting black  screens that makes me feel good it does  Heather Eric's West Global News Calgary  and that is global national for this  Tuesday I'm donor Friesen thanks for  watching hope to see you here again  tomorrow take care of yourselves  [Music]  you
 

